TEXT -32 -336 Left 3 ;#83 Nonlinear mixing in a single diode (illustrative, not Alan's bench circuit)
TEXT -32 -264 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mm7WfVzr1ao
TEXT -32 -216 Left 2 ;One diode is enough to mix: its curvature multiplies the two tones, and 7.455 MHz
TEXT -32 -176 Left 2 ;against 7 MHz leaves a 455 kHz difference, the classic AM intermediate frequency.
TEXT 640 -48 Left 2 ;Rif and Cif roll off above about 1.6 MHz, so the
TEXT 640 -16 Left 2 ;difference product survives and the sum does not.
TEXT 640 48 Left 2 ;Frequencies, levels and the 1N4148 are illustrative:
TEXT 640 80 Left 2 ;Alan's bench mixer is the NE602A board in circuits 01 and 02.
